    "fact_rationales": {
      "F10": "The presence of a cystic mass above the left atrium on the contrast-enhanced CT scan is not typical of myocardial infarction or acute coronary syndrome, but could be related to other conditions such as pheochromocytoma.",
      "F6": "The electrocardiogram findings of sinus rhythm with diffuse ST-segment depression and ST elevation in lead aVR are more typical of myocardial infarction and acute coronary syndrome.",
      "F8": "The elevated cardiac troponin I level is a strong indicator of myocardial infarction and acute coronary syndrome.",
      "F9": "The transthoracic echocardiography findings of diffuse hypokinesis of the left ventricle are more typical of myocardial infarction and acute coronary syndrome."
